GUIDES={
 'reader-comparison':('Compare documents and retained versions','Documents or Disclosures > Compare documents or versions: choose permitted originals/transcripts, optionally include permitted history, then select two to four resources across the server-paged sets. Open the comparison. Each pane checks its own access and offers Evidence text, Document or both, its own location selector and search. A blocked pane grants no access to another original. Citation anchors identify immutable versions and actual retained offsets; geometry and original-to-sanitized maps are unavailable where not established. Pages and lines are independent; this is not a semantic redline. Current readers support PDF, DOCX, XLSX, CSV and UTF-8 text; bounded XLSM, XBRL/iXBRL and EML body/attachment staging are supported; legacy XLS/MSG/PST/OST remain unsupported. External users see only sources they are explicitly entitled to or approved sanitized transcripts. Access is rechecked every 15 seconds.'),
 'financial':('Financial facts, verification and comparisons','Financial Evidence: select a confirmed source or approved sanitized transcript, choose the exact numeric token, optionally select header/label evidence locations, and enter literal entity, metric, currency, scale, period, accounting and consolidation labels. Verify interpreted dates, scale, numeric notation and decimal convention independently. New XLSX/CSV sources retain literal cell strings and anchors; formula expressions/caches are unverified and never executed. Original-source facts remain internal. A different lawyer verifies the dimensions; an independent SME releases only facts tied to an independently released sanitized derivative. Administration > Financial access enables the matter bank feature (default off) without granting content access. Bank facts still pass current document PDP, expiry, wall, approval and fact-release checks. Typed filters require currency for ranges. Compare two verified facts only when their dimensions match; exact Decimal differences preserve both records and never infer FX or an authoritative source. Conflicting comparisons create a deduplicated retained case. A different source-cleared SME may prefer a source or retain the conflict unresolved with rationale; both facts remain unchanged. This baseline has no automatic table extraction or financial materiality/hotness scoring.'),
 'retrieval':('Search modes and cited evidence','Questions defaults to Automatic/BM25 with no provider call. Lexical BM25 ranks only authorized chunks, including exact identifiers and bilingual risk-term expansion. Internal users can explicitly choose Semantic or Hybrid when the provider and independently approved cloud-processing policy permit it; those modes reserve up to $2 under the shared $10-month cap and never retry automatically. Source embeddings are cached with exact source/policy/text/model bindings. A failed request keeps its key; starting another provider request is an explicit action. External users search approved audience releases/transcripts only; external semantic indexing is not enabled; Financial mode uses explicit typed filters over verified facts and current external release entitlements. Ranking and top-k are not complete diligence or lawyer review. Stored corpus counts/ranks reauthorize their private source snapshots before display; revoked access denies old answers.'),
 'disclosures':('Sanitized document disclosures','Firm: open an original in Documents and expand Redaction & sanitized disclosure. Mark exact zero-based Unicode ranges; preview strike-throughs are proposals only. Submit a plan with audience, safe title, purpose, expiry and rationale. Another cleared lawyer accepts or rejects the exact plan. Complete whole-document review before Build & validate transcript. The server reconstructs a new PDF from sanitized extracted text, excluding original images, attachments, formatting, metadata and hidden worksheets. Native Word/Excel files are never released by this workflow. In Disclosures inspect the generated transcript and manifest. An independent senior Legal SME approves the exact output; clean-team content also needs a separate independently cleared antitrust counsel. External recipients see only approved artifacts for their organization and unexpired purpose. Questions cites only released transcript units. Changing source attributes or revoking approval denies future access, including saved cited answers; downloaded copies cannot be recalled. Original restrictions remain unchanged. Start/Stop use the existing API and reader.'),
 'content-labels':('Document and passage classification','In Documents open the existing evidence reader and expand Content labels & passage classification. Select overlapping labels for the current evidence unit/range or the whole document. Offsets are zero-based Unicode characters. Sensitive labels require active membership in the exact named clean-team scope. Add a rationale and propose. Proposed restrictions apply immediately to the whole original and its derived outputs; an independent source-cleared SME can confirm, and a cleared lawyer can contest without weakening protection. Bank eligible never grants access. Changed attributes invalidate old external release snapshots and create durable counsel-review impacts. Existing downloaded copies cannot be revoked. Restriction removal, physical redaction and sanitized derivative publication remain unavailable. Language is not governing law; no AI classification provider is enabled by this screen.'),
 'sla-alerts':('Scoped operational escalation','Open Documents, select a source and expand Source work. Bind a published SLA to an open task. In Scoped escalation plans, the creator or a scoped SME proposes explicit source-cleared recipients and a warning threshold. A different scoped Legal SME approves the exact plan. The existing worker scans bounded batches every 30 seconds; superseded bindings, changed source policy, closed tasks and frozen matters do not generate alerts. My operational SLA alerts is recipient-only. Mark read does not acknowledge; acknowledgement and creator/SME closure each require a rationale. No email, legal approval, automatic reassignment or release occurs.'),
 'review-clocks':('Reader timing and operational SLA','Start your assigned review task, open its evidence reader and explicitly Enable interaction timing. Only bounded, server-timed gesture-supported intervals count as active estimates. Quiet reading may be unobserved; idle is recorded after the pinned threshold. Hidden/unfocused readers stop timing; delays or errors leave gaps. Stop timing before signing. These estimates are not verified work or billing records. Admins/SMEs use Review SLA to record calendar versions, working hours, explicit holidays and a draft budget/idle threshold. Another Legal SME approves submitted policies; publish the exact version, then a task manager explicitly attaches it prospectively. New assignments require a new binding. Old records and calendar versions remain immutable. Root Admin alone cannot see source-specific activity. Missing timing and unconfigured SLA remain unknown, not zero or overdue.'),
 'review-work':('Custodians, parties and parallel review tasks','In Firm > Documents, choose an exact document version in Custodians & review assignments. Record source people/mailboxes/departments/systems with provenance and optional known custody dates; reuse a custodian ID only when you may access its original source. Record contracting parties separately. Create parallel document-review, QC, specialist-legal, financial or AI-coordination tasks for cleared firm accounts. These assignments never grant access, approve findings or start AI. The assignee accepts, starts, pauses, resumes and completes a coordination task; its creator or a scoped SME may reassign, cancel, reopen or change the deadline with a reason. Each change retains an immutable event with server UTC time and a scoped in-app notification. View evidence records an opening for the assignee only; browser-open time is not active work. Open Your review notifications to mark receipts read. Earlier restrictions survive source relaxation. Historical versions are read-only; signing freeze blocks content changes. Use the opt-in evidence-reader timing control and Review SLA configuration for bounded interaction estimates and explicitly approved, prospective business calendars.'),
 'vdr-import':('VDR CSV mapping and folder ingestion','In Documents, optionally choose a synthetic vendor CSV (up to 100 rows / 256 KiB). Map Source ID, VDR index, folder and file name; map Doc ID if available or generate a stable key. Save mapping & check rows retains an immutable mapping version, batch and original rows. Quarantined rows cannot ingest. Choose the matching document folder below and review version matches before import. Existing document identities, source bytes, hashes and reader links remain unchanged. Repeated CSV/file uploads do not duplicate source versions. Raw vendor extras and reviewer/risk/QC values are staged proposals, never access rules or approved legal decisions. Only the uploader with current matter and source permissions may retrieve staged batches; bank/client portals have no import access. Later assignment and checklist workflows will apply their governed fields separately.'),
 'checklists':('DD checklist scope and coverage','Open DD Checklist in the Firm portal or Administration. A Root Admin or Legal SME creates a draft from the audited A–N section map and one original material-contract request. The author submits it; a different scoped Legal SME approves it; the publisher publishes the exact hash. Lawyers record linked evidence and coverage with rationale. Verified requires whole-document review; a gap is not a legal finding or proof of missing company records. N/A needs a separate request and independent SME decision. PARTIAL requires responsive sources and a missing-information explanation. Waivers require independent SME approval. Expand Request log for retained follow-ups and source-bound references; unlinked notes are author-only. Reports show exact internal coverage snapshots without exposing them in external text. Earlier source restrictions and all decisions are retained. Replacement publication is blocked until the impact adapter is implemented. This foundation does not run LangGraph or call AI.'),
 'released-trackers':('Your released Excel trackers','Open Trackers, choose your matter and download an approved workbook naming your account. Another person in the same organization does not automatically have access. Source documents, internal owner UPNs and evidence-passage columns are excluded. Use Collaboration to ask about released material. Revocation, changed sources, a wall or expired matter membership can stop subsequent downloads; downloaded copies cannot be recalled.'),
 'trackers':('Tracker import and recipient release','In Diligence Trackers choose a matter, then Excel exchange. Download the coverage, risk or consent template. Keep RecordID and ExpectedRevision unchanged; edit amber fields. Upload a synthetic XLSX, inspect every row and select only valid proposals. Attest your review and apply with a rationale; database revisions and exact original evidence are retained. Then select reviewed records and a named Halden or Castlegate recipient. Edit audience wording if needed, create a draft and obtain independent approval of that exact workbook. Clean-team content additionally requires a separate cleared antitrust approval. A changed source/finding needs a new package and approval. Downloads are recipient-filtered by the same central policy engine. Use Risk Review to create findings or change legal reasoning/evidence.'),
 'action-center':('Legal SME change-impact workflow','In Playbook Management open a published legal playbook and Create replacement draft. Edit, test, submit, independently approve and publish. Publication records a durable assessment request, never a rerun. Open Action Center: inspect the exact field diff and permitted document task, Claim task, then approve or reject with a rationale and the exact snapshot. Reassess changed snapshots. The worker creates new candidate findings while preserving old reviewed/released history. Confirm/correct/reject candidates, record each comparison disposition, then close with justified release follow-up. Opening/acknowledging notifications is not approval. Overdue tasks produce a retained escalation and refreshed unread alerts; signing freeze blocks content/task changes. A shared fixture password represents synthetic role separation only, not independent real-world approval.'),
 'profile':('Your profile and password','Use the upper-right profile button to see the current authenticated UPN, name, employee ID, organization, roles and permitted active clean-team scopes. Copy UPN helps identify test accounts. Change password requires the current password and matching new passwords of 15–256 characters; the current session rotates and other sessions are signed out. Administrators manage names and employee IDs in Administration > Accounts. Tabs on one portal share a cookie; use a separate browser profile for independent test users. Account or authorization changes detected on focus or the 15-second check reload the workspace.'),
 'report-qa':('Report drafting and cited questions','Open Reports & Board Pack, choose reviewed findings and save a draft. Optional AI drafting creates a new unapproved version while preserving the saved source references and annexes. Edit and save, then obtain independent full-package approval. In Questions, retrieve permitted passages and inspect evidence; optional internal AI synthesis adds an unreviewed candidate, never client publication. Processing restrictions and the shared USD 2/10 caps still apply.'),
 'collaboration':('Client collaboration and intake','Choose an audience-approved package in Collaboration. Clients and bank users can submit questions/comments about their released material. Firm replies remain drafts until another cleared lawyer approves the exact text; clean-team-derived replies additionally require antitrust approval. Halden Uploads submits a synthetic folder to intake. A cleared firm lawyer accepts a separate immutable firm source copy, then confirms classification and arranges review. Uploading does not trigger AI or external release.'),
 'lifecycle':('Signing, closing and record custody','Propose a signing manifest after active jobs finish. Another fully cleared Legal SME approves the exact snapshot; content changes then close. At closing an independent Security approver closes external access. Client-copy deletion is a separate approved action and an active legal hold blocks it. Accepted firm source records and all audit history are retained. Protected local source archives reconstruct original bytes and extracted units. The operator can run scripts/verify_database_recovery.py --execute for an encrypted backup and isolated scratch restore; runtime files need separate preservation. No external WORM storage or portable key service is configured.'),
 'wall-checker':('Person and document ethical-wall checks','Open Administration → Wall checker. Select the client, optional client–matter pair and a person. SQL supplies the person’s roles and relationships. Client restrictions cover all matters; matter restrictions cover only that pair. Person + documents applies the shared document policy to each selected version and action. No recorded wall is not a conflicts clearance or access grant. Root sees decision-only policy references for restricted documents and gains no source access. Draft relationships or restrictions, then obtain independent Conflicts approval. Confirmed personal conflicts should use an unconditional named-person deny. Retirement also needs approval; history remains. Synthetic examples use client 054321, matters 100001/100002: lawyer03 is client-blocked, lawyer02 is blocked only from Beta, and lawyer01 has a mixed AI-processing document precheck. The checker itself never calls AI.'),
 'account':('Account and portal access','Sign in on your organization portal. Sessions are host-bound. Local role-testing profiles have three accounts per role, plus three named clean-team members, assigned to synthetic matter 012345-789012. Ask the operator for the appropriate account and shared demo password. Clean-team access is a matter/scope grant, not a separate portal. Credentials and tokens never belong in logs. Ask the local operator to reset or revoke access.'),
 'lawyer':('Lawyer review and release','For the walkthrough, use lawyer01@freshfields.example for ordinary/privileged intake. Open Documents, choose 012345-789012, upload a local Wave 2 file and choose its previous version if it is C001 or P001. Confirm declared handling, then ask a Legal SME to authorize analysis. The selected permitted matter follows navigation. Overview separates completed analysis, finding decisions and whole-document sign-off, and links outstanding reviews and release approvals. In Tasks & assignments, search current source-cleared work and use Manage source work for the existing coordination controls. In Risk Review, search the findings grid and choose Open review to fetch the exact assessment revision beside original evidence. In the Contract register, Open review fetches a fresh current contract/licence source profile; withheld prior metadata remains unavailable. Use Record whole-document review only after reading the entire document and deciding every candidate; this is not audience release. For each finding: correct the wording, assess severity/materiality, assign the next action and confirm or reject with rationale. Add lawyer findings where needed, including sources prohibited from AI processing. Diligence Trackers contains live contract, risk and consent registers. In Release Desk write an audience-safe summary; lawyer02 or another independently cleared lawyer approves the exact package. Reports & Board Pack creates editable drafts and local Word/PDF/Excel annex exports from reviewed findings. Another cleared lawyer approves the saved package; edits create a new version. Expand each section to inspect its retained reviewed finding and open current review separately. Compare saved versions from the same report history. Only released versions expose package/section discussion; firm replies still need independent approval. Diligence Trackers → Excel exchange supports validated imports and independently approved named-recipient exports. L002 is a deliberate AI-denial case: a cleared lawyer can read it and record a cited manual finding without an AI call.'),
 'sme':('Legal SME governance','Use sme01@freshfields.example for ordinary sources and the explicitly named sme03@freshfields.example for the synthetic pricing scope. Documents contains first-analysis authorization; Legal Governance shows persisted job status. Review the exact playbook hash and synthetic test results independently of its author. Approve or reject with rationale. In Playbook Management, load published versions, then authorize a synthetic analysis job with rationale. The queue processes authorized immutable source versions as well as embedded synthetic tests; inspect retained candidate evidence and job status. Questions retrieves original passages, and internal users can request an unreviewed cited AI answer under the shared spending cap. Reports can create optional AI prose from reviewed findings, preserving citation and annex versions. Collaboration contains drafts requiring independent approval before an external audience can read them. Offline failed or expired leases require an explicit recovery request, with a maximum of two attempts. Live AI requests are never resent automatically. The eight-risk checklist covers the required English/German topics; select it explicitly. Scanned PDFs require offline OCR, original-page transcript checking and recorded verification before analysis. Signing & Retention proposes a hash manifest for independent SME freeze; Security independently approves closing and client-copy deletion. Legal holds block copy deletion; firm records and audit history remain. Publication, historical reanalysis authorization and release are separate decisions. Partner title alone confers no role.'),
 'admin':('Administrative operations','START_KESTREL.bat launches PostgreSQL, trusted HTTPS Portal Home, pgAdmin, psql and five component CMD windows: API, redirector, database status, worker and health monitor. Ten-second pulses and sanitized activity are retained in .runtime/logs; current snapshots are in .runtime/status. STOP_KESTREL.bat closes the owned component tree and project database while retaining logs/data. Recovery is manual. No logs are automatically deleted. Accounts is a server-paged directory: Edit metadata loads an exact current revision before a two-field save. Registry has separate access and decision-history grids, a pinned command context and read-only direct/effective wall states. Pending/rejected matters remain administrable within current management scope. Inspect unknown creation/command outcomes before another request. Root Admin cannot approve their own legal changes, authorize SME jobs or override walls.'),
 'security':('Security/privacy approval','Review hosting region, AI-processing and external-sharing restrictions. Approve exact policy versions independently. No external provider is authorized merely by enabling an adapter.'),
 'conflicts':('Conflicts approval','Review ethical-wall policy drafts independently. Explicit denies override assignment. Do not remove your own wall or disclose restricted matter metadata.'),
 'clean-team':('Named clean-team workflow','Walkthrough: cleanteam01 ingests pricing; sme03 authorizes analysis; a cleared lawyer reviews evidence and drafts a sanitized summary; antitrust01 approves exact sanitization; cleanteam02 independently approves audience release. All usernames use freshfields.example. Only active named matter/scope grants permit restricted work. Derived outputs inherit restrictions. Lawyer review does not declassify content; separate antitrust approval may be required. Only appropriately cleared auditors/counsel can export the wider timeline.'),
 'external':('Released client and bank views','Open Overview and select 012345-789012, then Released Findings or Commercial Findings. The first-wave fixture contains one independently approved package for each audience. Only audience-released material is eligible. Bank access excludes privileged advice. Source downloads remain restricted. Reports lists the report versions approved for your audience with Word/PDF and Excel annex downloads. Questions retrieves quoted approved passages; Collaboration accepts questions/comments on an approved package. Firm replies need another cleared lawyer’s approval. Halden Uploads submits your folder to firm intake. Clean Team shows only individually approved source versions, with active named scope and unexpired grants.'),
 'audit':('Audit reports and retention','Ordinary users see permitted own activity. Designated auditors are matter-scoped. Choose category, optional matter and local-time bounds, then Apply audit scope. Scope edits clear old results and exports. Search, sort and page the server-authorized grid. The baseline window is limited to 1,000 permitted events before search. Export JSONL/CSV/HTML/PDF ZIP buttons include all filtered events across pages with a matching manifest. Hash verification is not WORM storage. PDF uses the same permitted selection and integrity manifest. External WORM remains unconfigured; local source archives verify source recovery only. No automatic deletion is configured.')}


GUIDES.update({
 'sme-profile-approval':('Approve AI stage profiles','Sign in with a source-cleared Legal SME account different from the profile author. In Administration > Agent Registry, select the validated matter and each submitted retained profile revision. Inspect the exact configuration and test/decision history, enter an independent rationale, affirm the review checkbox, then approve or reject that exact version. Repeat for contracts, drafter and quality. Root Admin publishes only after independent approval. Excel completion does not record an application decision.'),
 'ddr-runs':('Governed report drafting','Open DDR Runs, select the validated matter, then choose the published playbook and lawyer-reviewed findings. Offline mode is a deterministic workflow demonstration. Live mode additionally requires an enabled private OpenAI key and independently published contracts, drafter and quality profiles, with one aggregate $2 run ceiling inside the shared $10 monthly allowance. Submit once and watch the run pause for independent SME review. Open its complete report and Word draft, inspect evidence and annexes, then a different cleared SME records an exact-version decision. Internal approval does not release anything to Halden or Castlegate: use the separate audience approval workflow. Edited report versions require new internal approval; previous approved packages remain in history. Unknown provider completion pauses for reconciliation without automatic resend.'),
 'agent-registry':('Agent profiles and approved reruns','In Administration > Agent Registry, Root Admin prepares a versioned prompt/model/tool draft. Run the synthetic configuration checks, submit it, and obtain an independent Legal SME decision before publication. Only implemented roles/tools can execute. Material replacement creates protected impact tasks and notifications. Reading or acknowledging a notification is not rerun approval. A cleared independent SME approves the exact impact snapshot; the separate Queue approved rerun action creates a new draft run and preserves historical findings and approvals.'),
 'tables':('Inventory filters and saved queries','Use Documents inventory, Financial Evidence, Tasks & assignments, Risk Review or the current contract/licence register to search, sort, filter columns and page permitted rows. Tasks/findings use their own protected datasets; the Contract register reuses inventory. Saved queries retain inventory or financial evidence only. Select at most100 rows for internal metadata CSV/Excel export. Save the current query privately; bind selected evidence when the configuration contains source-derived content. Internal named sharing requires a separate independent review and expiry. Loading a saved query does not grant row access; current walls, source restrictions and releases are checked again. Column hiding is a display preference.'),
 'intelligence':('Clusters, signals and follow-up alerts','Open Review Intelligence and choose the permitted matter and view. Click the wheel or group list to drill down, then open source evidence from a row. Delay, legal and financial scores are separate; UNKNOWN means no eligible evidence. A Root Admin can draft operational weights, while an independent SME approves publication. Explicit scans under approved profiles create deduplicated source-bound follow-up tasks; read, acknowledge, escalate and close are separate events. Bank views need both feature gates and each released fact entitlement; internal staff productivity is excluded.'),
 'structured-intake':('Structured financial and email intake','Choose a folder, review the proposed files and declared handling, then explicitly import. Supported bounded formats include PDF, DOCX, XLSX, XLSM, text, CSV, XBRL/iXBRL and EML. Macros/formulas are never executed. Hidden or opaque content needs scoped restrictive handling. EML attachments remain staged inside the retained parent: download permitted inert attachments for separate explicit intake; no automatic child source is created. Unsupported legacy formats and unsafe active objects fail visibly. Confirm classification and verify OCR before analysis.'),
 'mfn':('Most-Favored-Nation playbook draft','MFN means contractual Most-Favored-Nation pricing/commercial parity. Download the new English/German synthetic draft, create a legal-playbook draft against the current published base, run its exact-definition examples and submit for independent SME approval. Publication of a material change triggers the existing impact and approved-rerun workflow. The22 examples test literal detection only; they do not establish legal applicability or accuracy. Competition counsel must review comparators, discounts/rebates, scope and exceptions. No source restriction is relaxed by adding this taxonomy.')})


def visible(db,actor):
    ids={'reader-comparison','financial','retrieval','disclosures','account','audit','profile'}
    roles=actor.roles
    if roles & {R.LAWYER,R.SME,R.ANTITRUST}:ids.update({'ddr-runs','tables','intelligence','structured-intake','mfn','content-labels','sla-alerts','report-qa','collaboration','lifecycle','action-center','trackers','vdr-import','review-work','review-clocks'})
    if roles & {R.ROOT_ADMIN,R.SME,R.LAWYER,R.ANTITRUST}:ids.add('checklists')
    if roles & {R.ROOT_ADMIN,R.SME}:ids.update({'agent-registry','sme-profile-approval','mfn'})
    if R.LAWYER in roles:ids.add('lawyer')
    if R.SME in roles:ids.add('sme')
    if R.ROOT_ADMIN in roles:ids.update({'admin','wall-checker','review-clocks'})
    if R.SECURITY in roles:ids.update({'security','lifecycle'})
    if R.CONFLICTS in roles:ids.update({'conflicts','wall-checker'})
    if actor.org.value in {'halden','castlegate'}:ids.update({'external','released-trackers'})
    named=db.scalar(select(CleanTeamMembership.id).where(CleanTeamMembership.account_id==actor.id,
        CleanTeamMembership.matter_id.in_(actor.matters-actor.walls),CleanTeamMembership.starts_at<=clock(),
        CleanTeamMembership.expires_at>clock(),CleanTeamMembership.revoked.is_(False)))
    if named:ids.add('clean-team')
    return ids


def guide_links(guide,org='firm'):
    if org!='firm':
        from kestrel.services.workflow_scripts import script_for,navigation_target
        from kestrel.deployment_settings import DeploymentSettings
        links=[];seen=set()
        for step in script_for(guide,org)['steps']:
            if step['portal'] not in {'current',org}:continue
            href=navigation_target(step,org,DeploymentSettings())
            if href not in seen:
                seen.add(href);links.append({'label':step['view'],'href':href})
        return links
    new={'ddr-runs':('DDR Runs','ddr'),'agent-registry':('Agent Registry','agent-registry'),'sme-profile-approval':('Agent Registry','agent-registry'),'tables':('Documents','tables'),'intelligence':('Review Intelligence','intelligence'),'structured-intake':('Documents','workflow')}
    if guide in new:
        from urllib.parse import quote
        view,api=new[guide]
        host='https://admin.localhost:8443' if guide in {'agent-registry','sme-profile-approval'} else 'https://firm.localhost:8443'
        return [{'label':view,'href':host+'/portal?view='+quote(view)},{'label':'Permitted API explorer','href':host+'/docs/'+api}]
    if guide=='mfn':return [{'label':'Download unpublished MFN draft JSON','href':'/api/v1/resources/playbooks/mfn-draft'},{'label':'Root Admin / SME: prepare legal draft','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/portal?view=Policies%20%26%20playbooks'}]
    if guide=='checklists':return [{'label':'DD Checklist','href':'https://firm.localhost:8443/portal?view=DD%20Checklist'},{'label':'Checklist API','href':'/docs/checklists'}]
    if guide=='trackers':return [{'label':'Diligence Trackers and Excel exchange','href':'https://firm.localhost:8443/portal?view=Diligence%20Trackers&tab=exchange'},{'label':'Excel tracker API','href':'/docs/trackers'}]
    if guide=='released-trackers':return [{'label':'Your released trackers','href':'/portal?view=Trackers'}]
    if guide=='action-center':return [{'label':'Open Action Center','href':'https://firm.localhost:8443/portal?view=Action%20Center'},{'label':'Create a replacement playbook','href':'https://firm.localhost:8443/portal?view=Playbook%20Management'},{'label':'Action Center API','href':'/docs/action-center'}]
    if guide in {'conflicts','wall-checker'}:return [{'label':'Person / document checker','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/portal?view=Wall%20checker'},{'label':'Checker API','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/docs/wall-checker'}]
    if guide=='clean-team' and org!='firm':return [{'label':'Read individually granted source versions','href':'/portal?view=Clean%20Team'}]
    if guide in {'report-qa','collaboration','lifecycle'}:
        views={'report-qa':['Reports & Board Pack','Questions','Risk Review'],'collaboration':['Collaboration','Uploads','Documents'],'lifecycle':['Signing & Retention','Audit']}[guide]
        from urllib.parse import quote
        return [{'label':view,'href':'/portal?view='+quote(view)} for view in views]
    firm='https://firm.localhost:8443/portal?view='
    if guide in {'lawyer','sme','clean-team'}:
        return [{'label':label,'href':firm+view} for label,view in [('Ingest and classify','Documents'),('Authorize and monitor','Legal%20Governance'),('Review citations','Risk%20Review'),('Release package','Release%20Desk')]]
    if guide=='admin':return [{'label':'Manage account names and employee IDs','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/portal?view=Accounts'},{'label':'Validate clients and matters','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/portal?view=Registry'},{'label':'Policy approval','href':'https://admin.localhost:8443/portal?view=Policies%20%26%20playbooks'}]
    if guide=='external':return [{'label':view,'href':'/portal?view='+view} for view in ['Overview','Questions','Collaboration']]
    return [{'label':'Portal Home','href':'https://localhost:8443/'}]


def guide_body(guide,org):
    if org!='firm':
        from kestrel.services.workflow_scripts import script_for
        script=script_for(guide,org)
        if script['variant']!='default':return script['status']+' '+' '.join(script['prerequisites']+script['limitations'])
    return GUIDES[guide][1]


def resource_response(db,request,prepare,guide_id=None):
    """Recheck current session and guide eligibility before emitting a download."""
    from kestrel.services.auth import authenticate
    db.expire_all()
    actor=authenticate(db,request)[2]
    permitted=visible(db,actor)
    if guide_id is not None and guide_id not in permitted:raise HTTPException(403,'Guide not permitted')
    result=prepare(actor,permitted)
    db.expire_all()
    fresh=authenticate(db,request)[2]
    current=visible(db,fresh)
    if fresh.id!=actor.id or fresh.org!=actor.org or current!=permitted:
        raise HTTPException(409,'Resources permissions changed; refresh before downloading')
    return result

@router.get('')
def guides(request:Request,actor=Depends(identity),db=Depends(database)):
    from kestrel.deployment_settings import navigation_url
    from kestrel.services.workflow_scripts import script_for
    def prepare(fresh,permitted):
        result=[]
        for k in sorted(permitted):
            script=script_for(k,fresh.org.value)
            result.append({'id':k,'title':GUIDES[k][0],'body':guide_body(k,fresh.org.value),
                'links':[{**link,'href':navigation_url(request,link['href'])} for link in guide_links(k,fresh.org.value)],
                'workbook_href':f'/api/v1/resources/{k}/workbook','step_count':len(script['steps']),
                'audience':script['audience'],'workflow_status':script['status']})
        return result
    return resource_response(db,request,prepare)


@router.get('/{guide_id}/workbook')
def workbook(guide_id:str,request:Request,actor=Depends(identity),db=Depends(database)):
    from kestrel.deployment_settings import settings_for
    from kestrel.services.workflow_scripts import MIME,workbook_bytes
    def prepare(fresh,permitted):
        content=workbook_bytes(guide_id,fresh.org.value,settings_for(request))
        return Response(content,media_type=MIME,headers={
        'Content-Disposition':f'attachment; filename="kestrel-{guide_id}-workflow.xlsx"',
        'Cache-Control':'no-store','X-Content-Type-Options':'nosniff'})
    return resource_response(db,request,prepare,guide_id)


@router.get('/{guide_id}/download')
def download(guide_id:str,request:Request,actor=Depends(identity),db=Depends(database)):
    from kestrel.deployment_settings import navigation_url
    def prepare(fresh,permitted):
        title=GUIDES[guide_id][0]
        body=guide_body(guide_id,fresh.org.value)
        steps='\n'.join(f"{i+1}. [{step['label']}]({navigation_url(request,step['href'])})" for i,step in enumerate(guide_links(guide_id,fresh.org.value)))
        return Response('# '+title+'\n\n'+body+'\n\n'+steps+'\n',
            media_type='text/markdown',headers={'Content-Disposition':f'attachment; filename="kestrel-{guide_id}.md"','Cache-Control':'no-store'})
    return resource_response(db,request,prepare,guide_id)


@router.get('/playbooks/mfn-draft')
def mfn_draft(actor=Depends(identity)):
    if actor[2].org.value!='firm' or not actor[2].roles & {R.ROOT_ADMIN,R.SME,R.LAWYER,R.ANTITRUST}:raise HTTPException(403,'Internal legal draft access required')
    from pathlib import Path
    data=(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]/'data/playbooks/contract_risk_en_de_v3_MFN_DRAFT.json').read_bytes()
    return Response(data,media_type='application/json',headers={'Content-Disposition':'attachment; filename="contract_risk_en_de_v3_MFN_DRAFT.json"','Cache-Control':'no-store'})
